[ti:2-10-材料作文]
[00:00.00]Currently,
[00:00.98]great achievements have been made in the field of artificial intelligence,
[00:07.27]which is taking over a good many human jobs.
[00:10.80]In the excerpt,
[00:12.08]the author assumes that since artificial intelligence can plan and organize for us,
[00:19.06]our brains will regress.
[00:21.12]Nevertheless,
[00:22.40]I disagree with the author’s opinion.
[00:25.54]I cling to the idea that our world won’t be like some science-fiction scenes where human brains are inferior,
[00:34.48]even if intelligent machines are getting increasingly smarter.
[00:39.89]To begin with,
[00:41.06]no matter how superior,
[00:43.03]artificial intelligence needs us just as much as we need it.It requires our supplies and repairs,
[00:51.09]hence our brains are going to catch up with the artificial intelligence.
[00:57.08]What is more,
[00:58.16]interactions between humans can never be replaced by machines.
[01:03.47]For intelligent machines,
[01:05.73]it is unlikely to develop human-like social competence which consumes a great deal of brain work.
[01:13.78]After all,
[01:14.67]with the development of artificial intelligence,
[01:18.89]human brains are also evolving.
